# winoracle (WARP, FL 11_0), 2026-09-28; the x86 build prints the same lines.
# Anisotropic reduction footprint as WARP measures it ([aniso], [reach]):
# ratio r <= 2 -> two probes (r-1)/2 texels either side of the coordinate;
# r > 2 -> N = effective MaxAnisotropy (largest power of two <= the value)
# probes r/(N+1) apart, outermost r(N-1)/(2(N+1)) away, along the major
# axis in texels of the sampled mip; each probe position is floored to
# 1/256 texel. Texture1D, Texture3D and cubes are filtered isotropically.
